ind the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+\\frac{1}{8}(4)^{2}]-[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{1}{8}(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ed73d23018f9c806ed118098310e29dda00b162774569f693186c676609b18e"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{14}{29}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{4}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{1-x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{1-x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm (-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-x|)+C \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ed73d23018f9c806ed118098310e29dda00b162774569f693186c676609b18e"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\frac{1}{1+x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{1-x}+\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+7"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-82619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-x)+7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between two points where $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula:\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=4\\sqrt{x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[4\\sqrt{x}]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+16x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=1+16x.$ Then, $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{16}\\text{d}u.$\n\nWe also need to compute new limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 3 \\\\ u & 1 & 49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{49}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{1}^{49}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{[\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}]|}_{1}^{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({49}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{343-1}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{57}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ed73d23018f9c806ed118098310e29dda00b162774569f693186c676609b18e"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{343}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{43}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{57}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{57}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-85596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{57}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-122287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-122287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{(1+{x}^{2})}^{1/2}\\cdot 2x=2x\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{2})}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[2x\\sqrt{(1+{x}^{2})}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2{x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=2{x}^{2}+1$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+x)|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(3)^{3}+(3)]-[\\frac{2}{3}(0)^{3}+(0)] \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-122287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ed73d23018f9c806ed118098310e29dda00b162774569f693186c676609b18e"} {"question" "q-122287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077006/state.json" "file_sha256" "b968579430d9326ad22623bab0b12c647395d4771fd7a630bbacff75ab8d5ac8"} {"question" "q-122287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] 